WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.760
The first thing you need to do when
integrating Torus to Canvas is to ensure

cue-2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:09.520
that OLI Torus is registered as an LTI
Advantage Tool in your institution's

cue-3
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.560
Canvas system. This is typically handled
by a Canvas administrator. If your Canvas

cue-4
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.300
admin hasn't integrated OLI Torus yet,
contact OLI support at

cue-5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.140
oli-help@cmu.edu.

cue-6
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.700
Okay, now to place the OLI Torus link to
Canvas, you have three options, the

cue-7
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:35.080
navigation menu, an assignment, or a
module. Adding OLI Torus to the navigation

cue-8
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.900
menu is recommended if you and students
need to enter it frequently. This will

cue-9
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.880
result in OLI Torus also being visible on
the Canvas class homepage. Adding OLI

cue-10
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:50.320
as an assignment is the recommended
placement. This allows you to place OLI in

cue-11
00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:54.320
your weekly curriculum and assign the
reading as homework or out-of-class

cue-12
00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:00.120
activities. Adding OLI Torus as a module
will allow students to navigate to OLI

cue-13
00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.920
through the module view. To avoid
confusion, add your Torus course link in

cue-14
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.620
only one place, navigation menu,
assignments, or modules.

cue-15
00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:15.360
Option one, add the link to the navigation
menu. Go to Settings at the bottom of the

cue-16
00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:20.620
Canvas navigation menu, click the
Navigation tab on the top, and scroll to

cue-17
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:26.780
find OLI Torus, not the other ones under
Disabled Items. Drag it up to the list of

cue-18
00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:31.940
enabled navigation items and click Save.
OLI Torus will now appear in your course's

cue-19
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:36.670
left-hand menu. Option two, add the link
in an assignment.

cue-20
00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:43.960
Click Assignments, Add Assignment, and add
a title. This is what students will see

cue-21
00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:47.920
when they click on Assignments in the
Canvas class. Scroll down to Submission

cue-22
00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.600
Type, select External Tool, click Find,

cue-23
00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:58.340
choose OLI Torus from the list, and click
Load in a New Tab. Click Save and

cue-24
00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:03.840
Publish or Save. If necessary, publish the
OLI Torus assignment by clicking the Not

cue-25
00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:09.940
Published icon on the right side of the
page. Option three, add the link in a

cue-26
00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:16.160
module. Click Modules in the nav menu.
Then create a new module. Give the module

cue-27
00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:21.400
a name such as OLI Torus Course, or base
the title on your Torus content, and click

cue-28
00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.340
Add Module.

cue-29
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.920
In the new module, click the plus sign and
select External Tool.

cue-30
00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:37.560
Select OLI Torus from the list, update the
title if you like, click Load in a New

cue-31
00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.100
Tab, and click Add Item.

cue-32
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.080
Publish the OLI Torus module by clicking
the Unpublished icon on the right end of

cue-33
00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:53.780
the OLI Torus module. And once you've
added the link to Canvas, it's time to

cue-34
00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:59.920
configure your OLI Torus course materials
for use with your students. Click the OLI

cue-35
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.920
Torus link you just added to load it in a
new tab and configure your OLI Torus

cue-36
00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:11.760
materials. Click Start and follow the
prompts. Select a source material to base

cue-37
00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:18.150
your course on. Use the search feature to
find the desired content if necessary. Now

cue-38
00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:22.500
enter basic info link, course name,
course section number, can be a catalog

cue-39
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.580
number or CRN, for example, and modality
for how class meets

cue-40
00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.750
and other course details.

cue-41
00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.680
Voila, your section has now been created.

cue-42
00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:39.780
Note that once set up, all links will
point to the same OLI Torus course no

cue-43
00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:44.090
matter where students access it from in
Canvas. Students have no OLI Torus

cue-44
00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:49.380
accounts. They will access everything from
the Canvas link. There you have it. In

cue-45
00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:53.820
just a few steps, you can add and
configure OLI Torus in your Canvas course.

cue-46
00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:57.160
If you need to unlink a course, contact
OLI support at

cue-47
00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:04.700
oli-help@cmu.edu.
